 "rule": "Hybrid cost rule (2c-c, latency of recipe h5), written 2026-10-31T19:33:31+07:00 before any latency or workload data of h5 models exists. Not from a source. Not reviewed by the user (user approval of 2026-10-31 for phase 2c). Same statements and approved numbers as experiments/npu/operator_support/onboard_g4b/ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0/rule.txt (5 percent, 2 session gap rule, 50 percent cycles), protocol P2 as there (not approved as the main protocol). The recipe h5 (float16 for the 15 box-decode tail tensors) recovered the INT8 accuracy in rule_recipes.txt experiment 2: SiLU css_test AP50-95 36.75 to 49.66 (FP16 49.76), ReLU 33.24 to 46.98 (FP16 46.49).\nQuestion: what does h5 cost in NPU latency and does it change the multi-core coverage, for SiLU seed 0 and ReLU seed 0, at CORE_0 and CORE_0_1_2?\nModels (INT8 files, sha256): \n  ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0 rknn_int8 a501f94ee391bab370c141bbc4853eb78c062635b0a01597fe3a9efb0d99e7dd\n  ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0 rknn_int8_h5 9658075e443e447408d1ee20da4d147e5df118242bee7b66337880e08ccb4dfa\n  ppe5_yolov8n_relu_100ep_s0 rknn_int8 c36458b70bfdf4d819078d9dbffd284e9cebf08c7b797d0270748b75a6db0b0f\n  ppe5_yolov8n_relu_100ep_s0 rknn_int8_h5 e2d11e13f7fe3b8c97ac04056752ff66f607c0674db905cf648d346b24533a56\nDesign: one interleaved run under P2 (as onboard_g4b): 16 sessions, for mask in CORE_0, CORE_0_1_2: silu-base, silu-h5, relu-base, relu-h5, the same order in both rounds, 45 s rest, benchmark_npu.py sessions (5 eval_perf without perf_debug, then 5 with perf_debug=True, --variant h5 for the h5 models). Realization as in onboard_g4b (helper log in pin mode, zero threads off CPU4, at least 99 percent of interrupts on CPU4), a model whose sessions are not all realized is 'ch\u01b0a k\u1ebft lu\u1eadn (P2 kh\u00f4ng th\u1ef1c hi\u1ec7n \u0111\u00fang)'. The driver aborts if a file changes.\nStatements per model (SiLU, ReLU) and mask: cost = median of the two session medians of h5 minus that of the deployed INT8, in ms and percent; '\u0111\u1ed5i latency' only when the absolute cost is larger than the larger of the two session gaps, and '\u0111\u00e1ng k\u1ec3' when the cost is at least 5 percent of the deployed INT8 latency (the approved 5 percent used as a materiality line). B for the h5 models by the rule of onboard_g4b (CORE_0_1_2 against CORE_0). A for the h5 models: a row is split when at least 2 of its 3 WorkLoad percentages are above 0.0 percent, coverage = split Total cycles over all Total cycles of the CORE_0_1_2 session, asserted equal to the sum of the h5 build table (build log in onboard_q2c/logs), '\u0111\u1ea1t' when at least 50 percent in every session. CPU ops and the dtype counts come from the build log tables.\nLimits: one run, two sessions per condition, one seed per model, h5 is one recipe (float16 box-decode tail), the box branch in h6 was not usable (lower accuracy), P2 not approved.\nBudget: experiment 1. Experiment 2 only if a condition was not realized.\n",
